{
  "id": "80546",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Integrated Rate Laws: Zero-Order Reactions",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For zero-order reactions, the rate law is:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "cviivgmtrlaxncz",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "08vhsj3gbq4xmis",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "l9cmttm3a892azt",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack^0\\;=\\;k",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A zero-order reaction thus exhibits a constant reaction rate, regardless of the concentration of its reactants."
              }
            ],
            "id": "bkizvq1ahcct0d9",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "zreo4vkyrp0bgz0",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0haec3ni5pzomfh",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "bfms30dzfi0d09n",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "tv0myjyyhriybn6",
            "items": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2202637683",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "An equation relating concentration and time can be derived for a zero-order reaction and shown to be:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "921726304",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;=\\;-\\;kt\\;+\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "where "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "k"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = rate constant, [A]0 = initial concentration, [A]"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "t"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = concentration present after any given time, and "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "t"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = time ."
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "448242965",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "dd"
              }
            ],
            "title": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " Integrated Rate Law for Zero-Order Reactions "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "337354850",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "type": "dl"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "1okza9atb1pte8q",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "bxw9m1r0lhyyan7",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The integrated rate law for a zero-order reaction also has the form of the equation of a straight line:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "9yf1pc17uar46r7",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "alt": "Two equations are written, one above the other, with arrows showing relationships between the quantities in the equations. The equation in the \n            upper line is “brackets capital A sub t equals negative k times t plus brackets capital A sub zero”.  The equation in the lower line is “y equals \n            negative m times x plus b”. The leftmost arrow points from “y” to “brackets capital A sub t”, the next arrow to the right points from “m” to “negative \n            k”, the next arrow to the right points from “x” to “t”, and the rightmost arrow points from “b” to “brackets capital A sub zero”.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "pjb1gb13jvbowha",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "height": 120.97500610351562,
            "id": "uc4pwc74geirvs2",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/9d/9d888b0c14193c2f7dc77b88f0f6e406/zero_order_line.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 242.96876532303762
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A plot of [A] (on the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "y"
              },
              {
                "text": "-axis) versus "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": " (on the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": "-axis) for a zero-order reaction results in a straight line with a slope equal to −"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "k"
              },
              {
                "text": " and an intercept of [A]"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "0"
              },
              {
                "text": ". If a set of data are plotted in this fashion but do not result in a straight line, the reaction is not zero order in A."
              }
            ],
            "id": "4ltaigpmhnf50fi",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The following graph shows a plot of ammonia concentration, [NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "], versus "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": " for the decomposition of ammonia on a hot tungsten wire and for the decomposition of ammonia on hot quartz (SiO"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "). The decomposition of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " on hot tungsten is zero order; the plot is a straight line. The decomposition of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " on hot quartz is not zero order (it is first order). From the slope of the line for the zero-order decomposition of ammonia on tungsten, we can determine the rate constant:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "6rz20z0br1ryldb",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "58p61yr7ys6cmxj",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0q2m6zwbg3ix7m2",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Slope}=-k=1.3\\times10^{-6}\\;\\mathrm M/\\mathrm s",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "hefu7bcb9lb8sj9",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "r9fmgsrvk9624ji",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "k\\;=\\;-\\mathrm{slope}\\;=\\;-\\left(-1.3\\times10^{-6}\\;\\mathrm M/\\mathrm s\\right)\\;=\\;1.3\\times10^{-6}\\;\\mathrm M/\\mathrm s",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "alt": "A graph is shown with the label, “Time ( s ),” on the x-axis and, “[ N H subscript 3 ] M,” on the y-axis. The x-axis shows a single value of \n            1000 marked near the right end of the axis. The vertical axis shows markings at 1.0 times 10 superscript negative 3, 2.0 times 10 superscript \n            negative 3, and 3.0 times 10 superscript negative 3. A decreasing linear trend line is drawn through six points at the approximate coordinates: \n            (0, 2.8 times 10 superscript negative 3), (200, 2.6 times 10 superscript negative 3), (400, 2.3 times 10 superscript negative 3), (600, 2.0 times \n            10 superscript negative 3), (800, 1.8 times 10 superscript negative 3), and (1000, 1.6 times 10 superscript negative 3). This line is labeled \n            “Decomposition on W.” A decreasing slightly concave up curve is similarly drawn through eight points at the approximate coordinates: (0, 2.8 times \n            10 superscript negative 3), (100, 2.5 times 10 superscript negative 3), (200, 2.1 times 10 superscript negative 3), (300, 1.9 times 10 superscript \n            negative 3), (400, 1.6 times 10 superscript negative 3), (500, 1.4 times 10 superscript negative 3), and (750, 1.1 times 10 superscript negative 3), \n            ending at about (1000, 0.7 times 10 superscript negative 3). This curve is labeled “Decomposition on S i O subscript 2.”",
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "The decomposition of NH"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " on a tungsten (W) surface is a zero-order reaction, whereas on a quartz (SiO"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": ") surface, the decomposition is a first-order reaction."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "dx41iu7i91w2c19",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "69tn6hx9h3pi4bo",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/40/4003a212d78de84f5b7a7279eddc3ef8/CNX_Chem_12_04_AmDecomK.jpg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "500"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "1245321481",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "665668589",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The following reaction is zero order and has a rate constant of 0.000978 M/s:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "j2q23liak9triog",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "2cvp43x85h4yjc3",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "zs5ccr77su5i0rp",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm A\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{products}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The initial concentration of A is 0.150 M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "45wt231rxi3mm13",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " What is the concentration of A after 2.00 minutes?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "38jmqytdtqdd4ex",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " How long will it take for the concentration of A to decrease to 0.100 M?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cc5gyw5lmh6hwz0",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We use the integrated form of the rate law for a zero-order reaction:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wl6w3dv4a0ustog",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "e3hkksdk6l7zpkw",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "5f5yqfxbmvg0xzq",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;=\\;-kt\\;+\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " We substitute the known values into the equation and solve for [A]"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "t"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "46uo90x2s3mq5dh",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "4u9rsehaoikanv9",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "dev2y6fehmq48f8",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;=\\;-\\left(9.78\\times10^{-4}\\frac{\\;\\mathrm M}{\\mathrm s}\\right)\\left(\\frac{60\\;\\mathrm s}{1\\;\\min} \\right)\\left(2.00\\;\\min\\right)\\;+\\;0.150\\;\\mathrm M\\;=\\;0.033\\;\\mathrm M",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that we needed to convert the time from minutes to seconds to cancel the time units in the rate constant."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "gtyx17ky3f0d2ab",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " We rearrange the equation to solve for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "t"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and substitute in the known values:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "9cnc8omi5msz7m7",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "x7s5odv6k6npe40",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3eq4r5r1lml56gu",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;=\\;-kt\\;+\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A{\\rbrack_0\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;{kt\\; =\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0-\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;t\\; =\\;\\frac1k\\left({\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0-\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\right)}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "gybj53j2ystn2v7",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u33txxas6wl5v7z",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "t\\;=\\;\\frac1{\\left(9.78\\times10^{-4}\\;\\mathrm M/\\mathrm s\\right)}\\;\\left(0.150\\;\\mathrm M\\;-\\;0.100\\;\\mathrm M\\right)\\; =\\;51.1\\;\\mathrm s",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3837447262",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "922184394",
